<%#
kind: PXEGrub2
name: AlmaLinux 10 bootc PXEGrub2
model: ProvisioningTemplate
oses:
- AlmaLinux 10
description: |
  UEFI (PXEGrub2) boot entry for AlmaLinux 10 image-mode (bootc) provisioning.

  The bootc payload is installed by `ostreecontainer` in the kickstart, but
  Anaconda's installer RUNTIME (stage2 = images/install.img) still has to be
  fetched over the network. We supply it as `inst.stage2=<medium_uri>`, where
  `medium_uri` is the jail-safe renderer macro for the install tree (the synced
  AlmaLinux 10 BaseOS kickstart repo selected on the host). The OS-method form
  `@host.operatingsystem.medium_uri` does NOT exist in this Katello.

  ks= / network / BOOTIF and any `kickstart_kernel_custom_options` host param
  come from the stock `kickstart_kernel_options` snippet, exactly like the
  default PXEGrub2 template.

  NOTE: UEFI (linuxefi/initrdefi) variant — the VM must use OVMF firmware.
  Legacy BIOS hosts need a PXELinux template instead.
%>
set default=0
set timeout=10

menuentry 'Provision <%= @host.name %> (AlmaLinux 10 image-mode)' --id provision {
  linuxefi <%= @kernel %> <%= pxe_kernel_options %> inst.stage2=<%= medium_uri %> <%= snippet("kickstart_kernel_options").strip %>
  initrdefi <%= @initrd %>
}
